    "question": {
      ":question/id": "be52e22c-32bc-5bfe-aacf-131d4f51fc1f",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $J$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\n- $L$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero. It is also an identity matrix; identity matrices are diagonal matrices.\n\nTherefore, only $J$ and $L$ are diagonal matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "b1b8346f-4c34-5703-958c-be4c153b2336",
