      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$F=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $F$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${f}_{31}=-1\\ne 0$.\n\n- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${h}_{21}=-1\\ne 0$.\n\n- $M$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 2 columns.\n\nTherefore, none of the given matrices are diagonal matrices.",
