    "question": {
      ":question/id": "379923f7-2a0d-5d7d-bccf-ab331540beed",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $H$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${h}_{12}=-1\\ne 0$.\n\n- $J$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $L$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 3 columns.\n\nTherefore, only $J$ is a diagonal matrix.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
